reviews.text:
ENSO has so many things going for it.

(1) The food is delicious;
(2) The mixed drinks are to die for;
(3) On Fridays and Saturdays, the DJ is mixing up dope beats like he's lost his mind;
(4) It's in the Epicenter, so, if you want to bounce to a club after getting some Miso soup and a seafood, you can walk upstairs and have your pick of five different nightclubs;
(5) The place draws people who are good-looking and, in some instances, will strike up random conversations with complete strangers.

What more could you ask for? If you sitting on the coach on a Saturday night and you start jonesing for some good music and good food, grab your wallet (or your purse) fire up the SUV and head to ENSO.

"Nuff Said,

Anti-Charisma
